    "extraction_status": "ready_for_resolution",
    "extraction_notes": "Text-layer table. Column grid and row bands recovered from the raster rule lines (pdftoppm -r 200); marks binned mechanically from pdftotext -bbox token centres and diffed against a visual read of the rendered page; no disagreement. TWO leading label columns ('Time' and 'Assessment'), so the first data column is position 3 and the 20 data columns run 3-22. Every assessment cell reads 'PK', so all six body rows carry the same activity_name; the within-visit timing that tells them apart is printed in the 'Time' row-label column and is carried as annotations t1-t6, one per row. Footnote marker 'a' on the 29/ET header is referenced but not defined on this page."
  },
  "table_metadata": {
    "table_id": "table-003",
    "table_number": 3,
    "table_type": "domain",
    "table_title": "Table 1c. Schedule of Pharmacokinetic Assessments",
    "table_purpose": "Pharmacokinetic sampling on the same study-visit timeline as Tables 1a and 1b.",
    "page_start": 36,
    "page_end": 36,
    "track_label": null,
    "column_count": 20,
    "row_count": 9,
    "header_row_count": 2,
    "activity_row_count": 7,
    "notes": "Classified domain rather than subsidiary: the column structure is NOT finer than the main SoA - the 20 data columns are identical to Table 1a's (Screening, -2, 1 ... 55) - and the participants are the same subjects, so this is a further assessment category on the shared timeline. The finer within-visit timing (Pre HD, SDA + 10/30/60/90 min, SDA + 18 to 30 hr) lives in the 'Time' row-label column, not in the column grid, and 'PK' is not an activity row of Table 1a or 1b that this table breaks down. The call is recorded here because the PK-sampling / subsidiary ambiguity is close."
  },
